ll)","value":2513.22,"year":"2026-27","kind":"gbp"},{"label":"Band D \u2014 council's own element","value":2126.09,"year":"2026-27","kind":"gbp"}]}},"dossier":{"summary":{"summary":"Blackpool's year-end treasury report is routine and shows the council actively cutting borrowing costs, not adding risk. During 2025/26 it refinanced \u00a3110m of short-term borrowing into long-term debt to rebalance the book to a 50:50 long/short split, repaid \u00a35.93m of long-term loans, and deferred the rest of the year's capital borrowing requirement until rates look favourable. That mix cut the overall pooled borrowing rate to 4.26% from 4.58% the year before (General Fund pool 3.82%, HRA pool 4.47%). The treasury revenue account came in \u00a3830k over its \u00a326.666m budget (3.1%), driven mainly by an HRA interest shortfall (\u00a3392k) and lower loans interest receivable (\u00a3588k) after some loans were renegotiated at year-end; investment earnings were \u00a3242k. No CFR, year-end debt total, investment balances or prudential-indicator compliance detail are in this excerpt \u2014 those sit in Appendices 4a-4d, which are referenced but not included in the packet.","fy":"2025/26","as_of_doc":"Treasury Management Outturn for the Year Ended 31 March 2026","as_of_url":"https://democracy.blackpool.gov.uk/documents/s109419/Item 4 Treasury Management Outturn.pdf","as_of_date":"2026-06-15","signals":[{"code":"none","headline":"Modest 3.1% treasury revenue overspend (\u00a3830k on \u00a326.666m budget); no new net borrowing, pooled rate falling (4.58% to 4.26%)","why":"Nothing in this outturn report points to distress \u2014 borrowing was restructured to reduce future cost, not increased."}],"key_figures":[{"name":"authorised limit","value":"\u00a3681m (total borrowing powers)","as_at":"1 April 2025","page":3},{"name":"loans refinanced","value":"\u00a3110m of short-term borrowing refinanced into long-term borrowing, to bring the book to a 50:50 long/short split","as_at":"2025/26","page":3},{"name":"loans repaid","value":"\u00a35.93m of long-term borrowing repaid","as_at":"2025/26","page":3},{"name":"pooled borrowing rate","value":"4.26% overall (down from 4.58% in 2024/25); GF pool 3.82%, HRA pool 4.47%","as_at":"31/3/26","page":3},{"name":"treasury outturn vs budget","value":"Net expenditure \u00a327,496k vs budget \u00a326,666k, an \u00a3830k (3.1%) overspend","as_at":"2025/26","page":5},{"name":"investment earnings","value":"\u00a3242k actual investment earnings from temporary investments","as_at":"2025/26","page":5},{"name":"hra interest pressure","value":"\u00a3392k in-year pressure from lower-than-expected HRA recoverable interest","as_at":"2025/26","page":5},{"name":"loans interest shortfall","value":"\u00a3588k shortfall in loans interest receivable, due to specific loans being renegotiated at year-end","as_at":"2025/26","page":5}],"commercial":null,"tms_components":null},"compliance":null,"documents":[{"title":"Item 3 Provisional Outturn report 2025-26","url":"http://democracy.blackpool.gov.uk/documents/s109404/item-3-provisional-outturn-report-2025-26.pdf","committee":"Executive","date":"15/06/2026","key":true},{"title":"Appendix 3c Ward Budgets 25-26","url":"http://democracy.blackpool.gov.uk/documents/s109407/appendix-3c-ward-budgets-25-26.pdf","committee":"Executive","date":"15/06/2026","key":true},{"title":"Appendix 3m Capital Outturn 2025-26","url":"http://democracy.blackpool.gov.uk/documents/s109417/appendix-3m-capital-outturn-2025-26.pdf","committee":"Executive","date":"15/06/2026","key":true},{"title":"EX24 Provisional Outturn report 2025-26","url":"http://democracy.blackpool.gov.uk/documents/s109746/ex24-provisional-outturn-report-2025-26.pdf","committee":"Executive","date":"15/06/2026","key":true},{"title":"Item 4 Treasury Management Outturn","url":"http://democracy.blackpool.gov.uk/documents/s109419/item-4-treasury-management-outturn.pdf","committee":"Executive","date":"15/06/2026","key":true},{"title":"Appendix 4d Outtur